### Article 10: Intellectual Property Rights

10.1 **Ownership of Content**: The Producer shall retain all intellectual property rights in and to the Content created under this Agreement, including but not limited to copyrights, trademarks, and any associated rights. The Distributor shall have a limited, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, distribute, and publicly display the Content solely for the purpose of fulfilling its obligations under this Agreement.

10.2 **Licensing of Third-Party Materials**: If the Producer incorporates any third-party materials into the Content, the Producer shall be responsible for securing all necessary licenses and permissions related to such materials. The Producer must provide documentation of these licenses to the Distributor upon request.

10.3 **Attribution**: The Distributor agrees to provide appropriate attribution to the Producer in all distributions and public displays of the Content, as stipulated in Exhibit D: Attribution Guidelines.

10.4 **Use of Trademarks**: Each party grants the other a limited right to use its trademarks solely in connection with the performance of this Agreement. Each party agrees to adhere to the trademark usage guidelines provided by the other party and shall not use any other marks without prior written consent.

### Article 11: Performance Metrics and Reporting

11.1 **Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)**: The parties agree to establish and monitor Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) to evaluate the success of the Content and associated advertising. KPIs may include viewership numbers, engagement rates, revenue generated from advertisements, and audience demographics. The specific KPIs will be outlined in Exhibit E: Performance Metrics.

11.2 **Reporting Obligations**: The Distributor shall provide quarterly reports to the Producer and the Advertiser detailing the performance of the Content, including but not limited to the metrics outlined in Section 11.1. These reports will include analysis and recommendations for future content and advertising strategies.

11.3 **Performance Reviews**: The parties agree to conduct bi-annual performance review meetings to discuss the reports and assess the effectiveness of the Content strategy and advertising placements. Adjustments to the Content or advertising strategy may be made based on the outcomes of these reviews.

### Article 12: Term and Termination

12.1 **Term**: This Agreement shall commence on the Effective Date and continue for an initial term of two (2) years unless terminated earlier in accordance with this Article.

12.2 **Termination for Convenience**: Any party may terminate this Agreement for any reason by providing thirty (30) days’ written notice to the other parties.

12.3 **Termination for Cause**: A party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if any of the other parties breaches any material obligation under this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within fifteen (15) days after receiving written notice of the breach.

12.4 **Consequences of Termination**: Upon termination of this Agreement for any reason, all rights and obligations of the parties shall cease, except for those obligations that expressly survive termination, including but not limited to confidentiality obligations and indemnification provisions.

### Article 13: Force Majeure

13.1 **Definition**: Neither party shall be liable for any failure or delay in performance under this Agreement if such failure or delay is due to causes beyond its reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, war, terrorism, strikes, labor disputes, government regulations, or power failures.

13.2 **Notification**: A party affected by a force majeure event shall promptly notify the other parties in writing of the occurrence of such event and its expected duration. The affected party shall use reasonable efforts to mitigate the effects of the force majeure event on its performance under this Agreement.

### Article 14: Assignment

14.1 **Assignment Rights**: No party may assign or transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other parties, except that the Distributor may assign this Agreement in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of all or substantially all of its assets, provided that the assignee agrees in writing to be bound by the terms of this Agreement.

