### Article 15: Intellectual Property Rights

15.1 **Ownership of Content**: All content created, produced, or otherwise developed under this Agreement (“Content”) shall be owned by Streamline Media Group, LLC. However, Global Broadcasting Network, Inc. shall retain the right to broadcast and distribute the Content as per the terms of this Agreement.

15.2 **Licensing of Rights**: Streamline Media Group, LLC grants Global Broadcasting Network, Inc. a non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, and display the Content in connection with its broadcasting and distribution activities. This license is valid for the duration of this Agreement and any extensions thereof.

15.3 **Third-Party Materials**: In the event that the Content includes any third-party materials (including but not limited to music, images, or proprietary software), Streamline Media Group, LLC shall ensure that all necessary licenses or permissions are obtained prior to the inclusion of such materials. Failure to secure these rights shall be deemed a material breach of this Agreement.

15.4 **Attribution**: All Content shall include appropriate attribution to Streamline Media Group, LLC as the creator of the Content, as outlined in Exhibit D (Attribution Guidelines). This attribution must be displayed prominently in all instances of broadcast and distribution.

### Article 16: Confidentiality

16.1 **Confidential Information**: For the purposes of this Agreement, “Confidential Information” shall include any data, information, or materials disclosed by any party that is designated as confidential, or that should reasonably be understood to be confidential given the nature of the information and the circumstances of disclosure.

16.2 **Obligations of Confidentiality**: Each party agrees to protect the confidentiality of the other parties’ Confidential Information with the same degree of care that it uses to protect its own confidential information, but in no event less than a reasonable degree of care. Confidential Information shall not be disclosed to any third party without the prior written consent of the disclosing party.

16.3 **Exceptions**: Confidential Information does not include information that (a) is or becomes publicly known through no breach of this Agreement; (b) is received from a third party without breach of any obligation of confidentiality; (c) is independently developed by the receiving party without use of or reference to the disclosing party’s Confidential Information; or (d) is required to be disclosed by law or regulation, provided that the receiving party gives the disclosing party prompt notice of such requirement and cooperates with the disclosing party's efforts to seek a protective order or similar remedy.

### Article 17: Indemnification

17.1 **Indemnification Obligations**: Each party (“Indemnifying Party”) agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other parties and their respective employees, agents, and affiliates from and against any claims, losses, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorney's fees) arising out of or in connection with (a) any breach of this Agreement by the Indemnifying Party; (b) any claim that the Content infringes upon any intellectual property right or other rights of any third party; or (c) any negligent or willful act or omission by the Indemnifying Party in connection with this Agreement.

17.2 **Indemnification Procedures**: The indemnified party shall promptly provide written notice to the Indemnifying Party of any claim for which indemnification is sought. The Indemnifying Party shall have the right to control the defense of such claim with counsel of its choice, and the indemnified party shall cooperate with the Indemnifying Party in the defense of such claim.

### Article 18: Governing Law and Dispute Resolution

18.1 **Governing Law**: This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York, without regard to its conflict of law principles.

18.2 **Dispute Resolution**: In the event of any dispute arising out of or relating to this Agreement, the parties agree to first attempt to resolve the dispute through informal discussions. If the dispute is not resolved within thirty (30) days, the parties agree to submit the dispute to mediation in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association. If mediation is unsuccessful, the parties may pursue binding arbitration in accordance with the rules of the American Arbitration Association, and the decision of the arbitrator shall be final and binding.

### Article 19: Additional Entities and Roles

19.1 **Content Review Committee**: A Content Review Committee shall be established, consisting of representatives from each party to oversee the quality and compliance of the Content produced under this Agreement. This committee will meet quarterly to review Content performance, discuss feedback, and propose adjustments to content strategies.

19.2 **Marketing Collaborations**: AdVantage Advertising Agency, LLC shall coordinate with Media Insights Analytics, LLC to develop targeted marketing campaigns aimed at maximizing viewership and engagement with the Content. This collaboration will leverage data analytics to identify audience segments and optimize promotional efforts.

19.3 **Performance Feedback Loop**: Media Insights Analytics, LLC shall provide quarterly performance reports detailing viewer engagement metrics, ratings, and other relevant analytics to all parties. This data will inform future content production and marketing strategies, ensuring alignment with audience preferences and trends.

