### Article 20: Intellectual Property Rights and Ownership

20.1 **Ownership of Content**: All Content created under this Agreement shall be owned jointly by Streamline Media Group, LLC and Global Broadcasting Network, Inc. Each party shall have the unrestricted right to use, reproduce, and distribute the Content in any media, worldwide, for the duration of the copyright, subject to the terms outlined herein.

20.2 **Licensing of Intellectual Property**: Any pre-existing intellectual property (IP) brought into the project by either party shall remain the sole property of that party. Each party grants the other a limited, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use such pre-existing IP solely in connection with the production and distribution of the Content developed under this Agreement.

20.3 **Attribution and Credits**: All Content shall include appropriate credits to the parties involved in its creation. Credits must be displayed prominently in accordance with the Attribution Guidelines set forth in Exhibit D. Any failure to provide proper attribution shall be considered a breach of this Agreement.

20.4 **Protecting Intellectual Property**: Both parties agree to take reasonable measures to protect the intellectual property rights associated with the Content. This includes but is not limited to filing for copyright registration and addressing any unauthorized use or infringement of the Content. The parties shall promptly notify one another of any potential infringements or unauthorized uses.

### Article 21: Confidentiality and Non-Disclosure

21.1 **Confidential Information**: For the purposes of this Agreement, "Confidential Information" shall include any proprietary or confidential information, whether written, oral, or electronic, disclosed by one party to the other in connection with this Agreement. This includes but is not limited to business strategies, financial information, and technical specifications.

21.2 **Obligations of Confidentiality**: Each party agrees to keep the Confidential Information of the other party confidential and shall not disclose it to any third parties without the prior written consent of the disclosing party. This obligation shall continue for a period of five (5) years following the termination of this Agreement.

21.3 **Permitted Disclosures**: Notwithstanding the above, either party may disclose Confidential Information if required by law or in response to a valid court order, provided that the disclosing party gives the other party prompt written notice of such requirement and cooperates in seeking a protective order or other appropriate remedy.

### Article 22: Additional Entities and Roles

22.1 **Legal Advisory Group**: A Legal Advisory Group will be established, comprising representatives from each party and external legal counsel, if necessary, to ensure compliance with all applicable laws and regulations related to the Content production and distribution. This group will meet bi-annually to review legal matters, including IP protections and compliance with advertising regulations.

22.2 **Quality Assurance Team**: A Quality Assurance Team shall be formed to oversee the final production and broadcasting of the Content. This team will consist of members from all parties and will be responsible for ensuring that the Content meets established quality standards and adheres to the guidelines set forth in this Agreement.

22.3 **Viewer Advisory Panel**: To foster audience engagement and feedback, a Viewer Advisory Panel will be created, comprising a diverse group of viewers selected from the target audience. The panel will provide insights into viewer preferences, content reception, and suggestions for improvement. The panel will convene twice a year, and their feedback will be integral to content development strategies.

### Article 23: Indemnification

23.1 **Indemnification Obligations**: Each party (the "Indemnifying Party") agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the other party (the "Indemnified Party") from and against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, costs, and expenses, including reasonable attorneys' fees, arising out of or resulting from any breach of this Agreement, including any claims of infringement of intellectual property rights or violation of applicable laws.

23.2 **Control of Defense**: Upon written notice that indemnification is sought, the Indemnifying Party shall have the right to control the defense of such claim with counsel of its choice, and the Indemnified Party shall cooperate with the Indemnifying Party in the defense of such claim. The Indemnified Party shall not settle any claim without the prior written consent of the Indemnifying Party, which shall not be unreasonably withheld.

### Article 24: Term and Termination

24.1 **Term of Agreement**: This Agreement shall commence on the effective date and shall continue in effect for a period of three (3) years, unless terminated earlier in accordance with this Article.

24.2 **Termination for Cause**: Either party may terminate this Agreement for cause if the other party fails to perform any material obligation under this Agreement and does not cure such failure within thirty (30) days of receiving written notice of the breach.

24.3 **Termination for Convenience**: Either party may terminate this Agreement for any reason upon providing the other party with thirty (30) days' written notice.

